WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.997
Coordination must cover the writers that
actually share authority.

2
00:00:03.997 --> 00:00:06.573
An asynchronous mutex can serialize access
to

3
00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:09.334
a cache owned by one Node.js process.

4
00:00:09.334 --> 00:00:11.542
Worker threads sharing memory need
suitable

5
00:00:11.542 --> 00:00:13.383
shared synchronization primitives or
message-based

6
00:00:13.383 --> 00:00:15.315
ownership; a promise-based lock in

7
00:00:15.315 --> 00:00:17.708
one isolate is not automatically shared.

8
00:00:17.708 --> 00:00:19.916
None of these local mechanisms coordinates

9
00:00:19.916 --> 00:00:22.677
another container or a direct database
writer.

10
00:00:22.677 --> 00:00:24.701
For database state, prefer constraints,

11
00:00:24.701 --> 00:00:26.818
conditional mutations, and suitable
